WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.920
How do you show that a protein keeps neurons alive?

2
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.300
You add it, and you take it away.

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.560
Each test shows something different.

4
00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:16.743
A mouse tumour grafted into a chick embryo drew in sensory and sympathetic fibres.

5
00:00:17.863 --> 00:00:20.343
Stanley Cohen purified the activity as a protein.

6
00:00:21.417 --> 00:00:25.077
The question here is what that protein does in a normal animal.

7
00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:27.437
Two words do the work.

8
00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:32.037
A factor is sufficient if it is enough, by itself, to produce an effect.

9
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.600
It is necessary if the effect does not happen without it.

10
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.600
Each experiment tests one of these, and no more.

11
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:41.790
Sufficiency first.

12
00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:48.390
In 1960, Rita Levi-Montalcini and Barbara Booker gave the purified protein to young

13
00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:49.390
mammals.

14
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.780
Their sympathetic ganglia were greatly enlarged.

15
00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:58.360
Injected into chick embryos, the factor makes sensory and sympathetic ganglia

16
00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.360
overgrow.

17
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:03.943
A bigger ganglion does not say whether neurons were saved or born.

18
00:01:04.783 --> 00:01:06.383
That needs counts, which come later.

19
00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:13.843
Now necessity. Cohen raised an antiserum, serum containing antibodies against one

20
00:01:13.843 --> 00:01:17.223
molecule. It blocked NGF's activity in culture.

21
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:23.697
Levi-Montalcini and Booker injected it into newborn mice, with rats and other

22
00:01:23.697 --> 00:01:24.737
mammals for comparison.

23
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:28.030
The sympathetic ganglia were destroyed.

24
00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.530
The procedure became known as immunosympathectomy.

25
00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:39.713
Predict. Give the same antiserum to older animals.

26
00:01:40.573 --> 00:01:42.773
Does it destroy their sympathetic ganglia too?

27
00:01:48.783 --> 00:01:50.223
It has much less effect.

28
00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:54.643
Dependence on NGF is tied to a developmental window.

29
00:01:55.683 --> 00:01:58.223
And the window differs between populations.

30
00:01:59.203 --> 00:02:03.403
NGF dependent sensory neurons are hit hardest by earlier exposure.

31
00:02:07.517 --> 00:02:09.497
But an antiserum carries a doubt.

32
00:02:10.317 --> 00:02:13.877
It might kill neurons by binding something on them other than NGF.

33
00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:18.867
So how would you remove NGF without using an antibody at all?

34
00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:23.470
Takeaway: adding NGF is enough to enlarge the ganglia.

35
00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.750
Taking it away shows it is necessary, if the antibody is clean.

36
00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:30.483
Settling that doubt took genetics.
